            <ArticleTitle>Reiter's Disease- Clinical Profile of Six Cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>108-111</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Common clinical features of 6 cases of Reiter's disease were chronic asymmetrical peripheral arthritis, keratoderma blenorrhagica, stomatitis, circinate balanitis, urethritis and back pain. HLA B 27 was found positive in three cases investigated. Two corticosteroid, unresponesie patients were managed with weekly methotrexate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
